@.str.205 = private unnamed_addr constant [76 x i8] c"show what packages and versions were added and removed between two closures\00", align 1
@.str.206 = private unnamed_addr constant [1582 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Show what got added and removed between two versions of the NixOS\0A  system profile:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix store diff-closures /nix/var/nix/profiles/system-655-link /nix/var/nix/profiles/system-658-link\0A  acpi-call: 2020-04-07-5.8.16 \E2\86\92 2020-04-07-5.8.18\0A  baloo-widgets: 20.08.1 \E2\86\92 20.08.2\0A  bluez-qt: +12.6 KiB\0A  dolphin: 20.08.1 \E2\86\92 20.08.2, +13.9 KiB\0A  kdeconnect: 20.08.2 \E2\86\92 \E2\88\85, -6597.8 KiB\0A  kdeconnect-kde: \E2\88\85 \E2\86\92 20.08.2, +6599.7 KiB\0A  \E2\80\A6\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command shows the differences between the two closures *before*\0Aand *after* with respect to the addition, removal, or version change\0Aof packages, as well as changes in store path sizes.\0A\0AFor each package name in the two closures (where a package name is\0Adefined as the name component of a store path excluding the version),\0Aif there is a change in the set of versions of the package, or a\0Achange in the size of the store paths of more than 8 KiB, it prints a\0Aline like this:\0A\0A```console\0Adolphin: 20.08.1 \E2\86\92 20.08.2, +13.9 KiB\0A```\0A\0ANo size change is shown if it's below the threshold. If the package\0Adoes not exist in either the *before* or *after* closures, it is\0Arepresented using `\E2\88\85` (empty set) on the appropriate side of the\0Aarrow. If a package has an empty version string, the version is\0Arendered as `\CE\B5` (epsilon).\0A\0AThere may be multiple versions of a package in each closure. In that\0Acase, only the changed versions are shown. Thus,\0A\0A```console\0Alibfoo: 1.2, 1.3 \E2\86\92 1.4\0A```\0A\0Aleaves open the possibility that there are other versions (e.g. `1.1`)\0Athat exist in both closures.\0A\0A\00", align 1
